# hugmesh-wiki-ui — runtime configuration, by example.
#
# NOTHING LOADS THIS FILE. There is no dotenv anywhere in this repo: the SPA is
# a static Angular build served by nginx and has no process environment of its
# own. This file is the checked-in enumeration the README's "Runtime
# configuration" section points at — copy the lines you need into the compose
# `environment:` block or the cluster ConfigMap that runs the image, or export
# them in your shell for the dev/test targets.
#
# EVERY VALUE HERE IS OPTIONAL. Unset means the shipped default, and the
# defaults are exactly what a plain `docker run` of this image already gets:
# there is no required configuration and no startup validation to fail.
#
# Commented-out values below ARE the defaults unless the comment says otherwise.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Browser globals — NOT environment variables
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The one browser-side knob this app has cannot be set from env, because the
# served SPA has no process env. It is a global the HOST PAGE must define
# before the federation bootstrap reads it:
#
#   <script>globalThis.__HUG_WIKI_URL__ = 'https://wiki-bff.example.test';</script>
#
#   __HUG_WIKI_URL__   Base URL of the wiki BFF, behind the WIKI_BASE_URL
#                      injection token (src/app/wiki.service.ts). Default ''
#                      = same origin, which is correct wherever the fe-gateway
#                      proxies /bff/wiki/** to hugmesh-wiki-bff-api. Applies
#                      uniformly to the content, access and attachments
#                      clients. That is the COMPLETE list of this app's
#                      browser globals — src/ declares no other
#                      __HUG_*__/__SNAP_*__ and reads no process.env.
#
# Nothing sets it today: hugmesh-host-shell assigns no __HUG_*__ global under
# its src/, and unlike login-ui this image ships no config-injection entrypoint
# hook (docker-entrypoint.d/40-snap-config.sh) to turn an env var into a
# pre-bootstrap global. So there is deliberately NO HUG_WIKI_URL variable in
# this file — adding one would document a contract that no code reads.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2. Container environment — read at start by docker-entrypoint.d/
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Read once before nginx forks, so a change is an env edit plus a restart,
# never an image rebuild.

# Theme token text — a ":root:root { --hug-*: ... }" block, written VERBATIM to
# the served stylesheet by 50-hug-theme.sh. Zero colour maths happens in shell,
# deliberately: the text is already derived by the single implementation in
# hugmesh-generator (studio/hugmesh_studio/core/theme.py). Unset => an empty
# stylesheet, so the compiled :root literals render the shipped brand.
#HUG_THEME_CSS=

# Where the hook writes it. Set in the Dockerfile and best left alone:
# nginx.conf aliases /hug-theme.css and /snap-theme.css to those literal /tmp
# paths, so repointing this leaves nginx serving nothing and the page silently
# unthemed. /tmp rather than the docroot because uid 101 on the unprivileged
# nginx image cannot write the docroot.
#HUG_THEME_OUT=/tmp/hug-theme.css

# Legacy spellings, accepted only until the fleet-wide SNAP_* -> HUG_* rename
# finishes (the producing half of that contract lives outside this image, so
# the two halves cannot flip in one commit). Used ONLY when the HUG_ name is
# unset; prefer the HUG_ names.
#SNAP_THEME_CSS=
#SNAP_THEME_OUT=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3. Build / test / tooling — developer + CI only
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# None of these reach a deployed container.

# Spec `npm run gen:spec` copies to openapi.json before regenerating src/app/api/.
#WIKI_BFF_SPEC=../hugmesh-wiki-bff-api/src/main/resources/openapi/openapi.json

# Headless browser for `npm test`. CI runs the same suite in a node:24-alpine
# + chromium container with CHROME_BIN=/usr/bin/chromium.
#CHROME_BIN=/opt/google/chrome/chrome

# `make pentest`: the DAST baseline target (unset => DAST is skipped cleanly)
# and where the shared harness is checked out.
#DAST_TARGET_URL=
#GENERATOR_DIR=../hugmesh-generator

# Playwright + Gherkin/BDD harness against a live stack (see e2e/README.md).
#E2E_BASE_URL=https://host.docker.internal:8443

# Seed-user credentials for that harness. THESE ARE SECRETS — export them in
# your shell or put them in the CI secret store; never fill them in here.
# Both are OPTIONAL overrides: a role resolves its own E2E_<ROLE>_PASSWORD,
# then the shared E2E_PASSWORD, then the run-state `.e2e-credentials` file
# hugmesh-generator's `make stack-seed` writes ($E2E_CREDENTIALS_FILE, or the
# file found walking up from cwd). There is NO literal default — with nothing
# resolved the harness throws naming `make stack-seed`. The per-role names
# come from e2e/tests/helpers/roles.ts.
#E2E_CREDENTIALS_FILE=
#E2E_PASSWORD=
#E2E_SUPERADMIN_PASSWORD=
#E2E_ADMIN_A_PASSWORD=
#E2E_ADMIN_B_PASSWORD=
#E2E_MOD_WIKI_PASSWORD=
#E2E_MOD_PASSWORD=
#E2E_USER_PASSWORD=
#E2E_READER_B_PASSWORD=

# GitLab's own CI_* variables, and the HOST_UID/HOST_GID the `test` job
# computes from id -u / id -g, are set by the pipeline itself — not knobs.
